\section{Results}\label{sec:results}

\subsection{What decides the adult comparison}\label{sec:res-adult}

With sensor noise alone, Neuromag led both OPM arrays: the median paired ratio over the << F.g2_n_targets >> targets was << F.g2_dense_vs_combined_int_ratio >> for the dense array and << F.g2_matched_vs_combined_int_ratio >> for the site-matched array (Fig.~\ref{fig:conditions}). Brain noise changed the comparison. With the room field included, it made up << F.g2_noise_share_dense_brain_pct >> of a dense-array OPM channel's in-band variance and << F.g2_noise_share_squid_mag_brain_pct >> of a Neuromag magnetometer's (room field, << F.g2_noise_share_squid_mag_room_pct >>). With sensor plus brain noise, the dense array's ratio was << F.g2_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> << F.g2_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci_3dp >> ($D$ = << F.wr_adult_dense_ib_db >>~dB), and the OPM was ahead at << F.wr_g2_ahead_n >> of the << F.g2_n_targets >> targets. The site-matched array's ratio was << F.g2_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> << F.g2_matched_vs_combined_ib_ci_3dp >> ($D$ = << F.wr_adult_matched_ib_db >>~dB), with no established advantage.

Which Neuromag channels and which SNR measure entered the comparison changed the number. Against the << F.g2_squid_grad_channels >> gradiometers alone, the ratios were << F.g2_dense_vs_grad_ib_ratio >> (dense) and << F.g2_matched_vs_grad_ib_ratio >> (site-matched), and against the << F.g2_squid_sites >> magnetometers << F.g2_dense_vs_mag_ib_ratio >> and << F.g2_matched_vs_mag_ib_ratio >>. By peak-channel SNR, the closest analogue of the sensor-level SNRs of clinical studies (Section~S1), the dense array was ahead of the magnetometers (<< F.g2_peak_dense_vs_mag_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_peak_dense_vs_mag_ib_ci >>) but behind the best of all << F.g2_squid_channels >> channels (<< F.g2_peak_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_peak_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci >>). By mean-power SNR, its lead was small (<< F.g2_meanpow_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >>).

The OPM noise floor decided the sign. From << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_min >> to << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_max >>~fT/√Hz, the dense array's ratio fell from << F.g2_sens_asd7ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> to << F.g2_sens_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> << F.g2_sens_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci_3dp >>, and the site-matched array's from << F.g2_sens_asd7ft_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> to << F.g2_sens_asd30ft_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >>. The break-even white noise was << F.rev_ns_breakeven_dense_vs_combined_ib_asd >> << F.rev_ns_breakeven_dense_vs_combined_ib_asd_ci >>~fT/√Hz for the dense array and << F.rev_ns_breakeven_matched_vs_combined_ib_asd >> << F.rev_ns_breakeven_matched_vs_combined_ib_asd_ci >>~fT/√Hz for the site-matched array (Fig.~\ref{fig:noise}D).

Over the ranges tested, other single changes moved the dense ratio less (Fig.~\ref{fig:conditions}). Projecting out the room field gave << F.g2_dense_vs_combined_proj_ratio_3dp >> << F.g2_dense_vs_combined_proj_ci_3dp >>, and the site-matched array then trailed Neuromag (<< F.g2_matched_vs_combined_proj_ratio_3dp >> << F.g2_matched_vs_combined_proj_ci_3dp >>). A << F.g2_opm_gap_small_mm >>- or << F.g2_opm_gap_large_mm >>-mm gap between OPM and scalp lowered the dense ratio to << F.g2_sens_gap3mm_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> or << F.g2_sens_gap6mm_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >>, and << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_max >>~fT/√Hz with a << F.g2_opm_gap_small_mm >>-mm gap reversed it (<< F.g2_joint_gap3mm_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> << F.g2_joint_gap3mm_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci_3dp >>). A triaxial array at the site-matched sites recovered much of the dense lead (<< F.g2_triax_equal_vs_combined_ib_ratio >>; << F.g2_triax_tang2x_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> with tangential axes twice as noisy). With a covariance estimated from << F.g2_plugin60s_samples >> independent samples, equivalent in time and bandwidth to << F.wr_cov_seconds_long >>~s of data, the ratios were << F.g2_plugin60s_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_plugin60s_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci >> (dense) and << F.g2_plugin60s_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_plugin60s_matched_vs_combined_ib_ci >> (site-matched), and a << F.g2_band_3_70hz_label >>~Hz band changed little (<< F.g2_band_3_70hz_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> and << F.g2_band_3_70hz_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >>). Across these conditions, the OPM noise floor and the array decided which system led, the comparator and the metric decided which reported number showed it, and depth changed the size of the dense lead and the sign of the site-matched array's (Section~\ref{sec:res-depth}).

